  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $I=\\int 2^{n}\\left[f^{\\prime}(x)+f(x) \\log 2\\right] d x$\r\n$\\begin{array}{ll}\\text { Consider } & g(x)=2^{x} f(x) \\\\ \\Rightarrow & g^{\\prime}(x)=2^{x} f^{\\prime}(x)+2^{x} f(x) \\log 2 \\\\ \\Rightarrow & g^{\\prime}(x)=2^{x}\\left[f^{\\prime}(x)+f(x) \\log 2\\right] \\\\ \\therefore \\quad & \\quad I=\\int g^{\\prime}(x) d x=g(x)+C=2^{x} f(x)+C\\end{array}$",
    "image": null
  },
